Article 2 (Processing of Sensitive Information, etc. by Prosecutors, etc.) Where unavoidable for the performance of any of the following duties, prosecutors and employees of prosecutors' offices may process materials containing sensitive information under Article 23 of the Personal Information Protection Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"), personally identifiable information under Article 24 of the Act, resident registration numbers under Article 24-2 of the Act, or other personal information:
1. Investigation of offenders, criminal facts and evidence thereof, institution and maintenance of public prosecutions under the Criminal Procedure Act;
2. Direction of judicial police officers and special judicial police officers concerning criminal investigations under the Criminal Procedure Act;
3. Execution of, and direction and supervision over the execution of, final and conclusive judgments under the Criminal Procedure Act;
4. Conduct of litigation in which the State is a party or an intervenor and administrative litigation under the Act on Litigation to Which the State Is a Party, or direction and supervision over the conduct thereof;
5. Duties concerning provisional measures, emergency measures, separation of victims from perpetrators, protection and assistance for victims and other persons involved in cases, processing of protection cases involving families, juveniles or children, and criminal mediation under the Act on Special Cases Concerning the Punishment of Crimes of Domestic Violence, the Act on the Prevention of Domestic Violence and Protection of Victims, the Act on the Prevention of Commercial Sex Acts and Protection of Victims, the Act on the Punishment of Arrangement of Commercial Sex Acts, the Act on Special Cases Concerning the Punishment of Sexual Crimes, the Child Welfare Act, the Act on the Protection of Children and Youth against Sex Offenses, the Act on Special Cases Concerning the Punishment of Child Abuse Crimes, the Juvenile Act, the Act on Probation, the Crime Victim Protection Act, the Crime Victim Protection Fund Act, the Act on Protection of Specific Crime Informants, the Act on Special Cases Concerning the Punishment of Specific Violent Crimes, the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities, the Act on Guarantee of Rights of and Support for Persons with Developmental Disabilities, the Welfare of Senior Citizens Act, the Immigration Act, the Act on Special Cases Concerning Expedition, etc. of Legal Proceedings, the Administration and Treatment of Correctional Institution Inmates Act, and other relevant Acts;
6. Duties concerning the collection, use, and protection of DNA identification information under the Act on the Use and Protection of DNA Identification Information, including collection of DNA samples for identification, registration of DNA identification information, applications for warrants for collection of DNA samples, registration and management of DNA identification information, searches and responses to inquiries, deletion of such information, and disposal of DNA samples;
7. Duties concerning criminal compensation and restoration of honor under the Criminal Compensation and Restoration of Honor Act;
8. Operation and management of prosecutorial information and communications systems, including the internal computer network of prosecutors' offices;
9. Personnel-related affairs, including appointment, awards and decorations, disciplinary action, applications for and issuance of personnel certificates for prosecutors and employees of prosecutors' offices, requests for verification of facts or data from relevant agencies or organizations, and secondment or appointment of persons who are not prosecution officials;
10. Duties concerning matters falling under prosecutors' authority pursuant to other statutes under Article 4 (1) 6 of the Prosecutors' Office Act;
11. Duties within the responsibilities of employees of prosecutors' offices under Articles 46 through 49 of the Prosecutors' Office Act;
12. Affairs incidentally necessary to perform the duties referred to in subparagraphs 1 through 11.
